    "category": "Non-automatic weighing instrument",
    "type_designations": ["XS Series", "XS 500"],
    "description": "The Avery Berkel XS is a mains-powered, Class III, price-computing, stand-alone non-automatic weighing instrument intended for direct sales to the public. It comprises a vendor's keyboard with 23 fixed keys and up to 59 programmable keys, a vendor's backlit LCD display with up to four numeric fields, one alphanumeric field and annunciators, an identical customer's backlit LCD display, an integrated printer with thermal print head, a two-piece plastic housing containing the load cell and electronics, a stainless steel load receptor and a level indicator. Devices: initial zero-setting (up to 20% of Max), semi-automatic zero-setting, automatic zero-setting and zero-tracking (up to 4% of Max), zero indicator, net indicator, semi-automatic subtractive tare balancing/weighing, preset tare, price computing, non-weighed items, totalisation, self-service mode of operation, and a price-labelling configuration in which printing below Min is not allowed. Interfaces: Ethernet (wired or integral Wi-Fi), USB, cash drawer. Alternatives: XS with tower-mounted customer display; XS with tower-mounted operator keyboard and double-sided display; XS connected to a remote customer self-serve keyboard (customer display may be disabled or removed); XS 500 utilising a hanging scale construction."
